'''Kiros''' was an idyllic [[Planet|world]] filled with vast [[Color|green]] valleys and flowing [[water]]falls<ref name="Kidnapped" /> located in the [[Kiros system]] in the [[the galaxy]]'s [[Expansion Region]]. Located in the [[Ehosiq sector]]<ref name="Appendix" /> like [[Shili]],<ref name="Shili system">{{GalaxyMapAppendix}} &mdash; Based on corresponding data for the [[Shili system]]</ref> the [[homeworld]] of the [[Togruta]] [[species]],<ref name="Togruta">{{Databank|togruta|Togruta}}</ref> Kiros was home host to 50,000 Togruta colonists. The planet was ruled by [[Governor]] [[Gupat Roshti]], who was contacted by [[Jedi Master|Master]] [[Yoda]] just prior to the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems|Separatist]] [[conquest of Kiros]] during the [[Clone Wars]].<ref name="Kidnapped" />

[[Count]] [[Dooku]] approached the Governor of the world to allow the Separatists to move the population to a secure location while they established a base there. [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]], [[Anakin Skywalker]], [[Ahsoka Tano]], and [[Clone Captain]] [[Rex]] later fought a [[Battle on Kiros|battle]] on Kiros, where they liberated the planet, but discovered that the entire population had been taken by [[Zygerrian Slave Empire|slavers]].<ref name="Kidnapped" /> After a [[Battle of Kadavo|battle]] at [[Kadavo]] had ended and the [[Zygerrian]] [[Kadavo slave processing facility|slave processing facility]] was destroyed, the former captives were returned to Kiros, to rebuild their society.<ref name="Escape from Kadavo">{{TCW|Escape from Kadavo}}</ref>

{{Planet-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
Kiros first appeared in the episode "[[Kidnapped]]," the eleventh episode of the [[Star Wars: The Clone Wars|''Star Wars: The Clone Wars'' television series']] [[The Clone Wars: Season Four|fourth season]].<ref name="Kidnapped" />

